Spec: specs/001-core-and-anthropic-passthrough/spec.md (AC30, AC36, AC38, AC48: the access-line half; the proxy fills Meta from T8 on)
Research: Q8 (access line lost on ErrAbortHandler)
Why this approach: the line is built in a defer without recover, so an ErrAbortHandler panic still reaches net/http untouched and a real panic keeps its stack for recoverer; Settle runs first in the same defer so the abort flags are decided from the inbound context before logging. Every proxy field is gated on Meta.Protocol, so /healthz, 404s and any handler that sets other fields but no Protocol keep the exact 000 key set. ttfb_ms uses the same microsecond-precision millisecond float as duration_ms.
Alternatives rejected: logging after next.ServeHTTP (the 000 shape, loses the line on abort, Q8); a recover in accessLog (would have to re-panic and would hide the original stack).
Trade-off / known limit: TestRecoverer_AbortHandler (000) asserted the abort left the log empty; Q8 and plan.md now require the access line on that path, so its assertion is narrowed to "no line other than the access line" (recoverer still logs nothing). upstream_aborted is only exercised here through a Meta the test sets, since the response watcher is unexported in core; the end-to-end case is AC48 in T9+.
